CHALLENGES
There are a nu mber of difficult ies in creating an A R wayfinder for a lib rary using datasets and libraries. First of all, because of elements like changing lighting and occlusions, it can be challenging to ensure accurate spatial mapping in a library setting. Integration of external datasets with the unique layout of the library may present calibration challenges. Maintaining the accuracy of the AR annotations is also a challenge in dynamic library spaces with furn iture that can be moved around or temporary displays. The integration of an effective dataset management system presents challenges in terms of storage, retrieval, and realtime updates when handling the variety of lib rary content and possibly large datasets.
CONCLUSION AND FUT URE WORKS
AR wayfinding in libraries offers a modern and efficient solution to the challenges of navigating books in large lib rary spaces. It enhances the user experience, improves accessibility, and provides opportunities for interactive engagement with library res ources. Users can simply fo llo w the virtual markers or arro ws displayed on their devices, eliminating confusion and reducing the t ime spent searching for items or areas within the library.

